{
  "case_id": "2018-17-9572",
  "document_hash": "6a47be7964533f8095630376d2ab79acec46a09f6b7615dfa0f3a12dad9a29ff",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2018-17-9572",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6a47be7964533f8095630376d2ab79acec46a09f6b7615dfa0f3a12dad9a29ff",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6a47be796453-0000-0002",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 10:16 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2018-17-9572",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6a47be7964533f8095630376d2ab79acec46a09f6b7615dfa0f3a12dad9a29ff",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6a47be796453-0000-0000",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In the first four trials, Mr. Evans exercised 36 peremptory challenges, all of them against African American jurors. In the sixth trial, he exercised five out of six of his challenges against African American jurors."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2018-17-9572",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6a47be7964533f8095630376d2ab79acec46a09f6b7615dfa0f3a12dad9a29ff",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6a47be796453-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The only plausible interpretation of all of the evidence viewed cumulatively is that Doug Evans began jury selection in Flowers VI with an unconstitutional end in mind, to seat as few African American jurors as he could."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MS. JOHNSON",
      "case_id": "2018-17-9572",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6a47be7964533f8095630376d2ab79acec46a09f6b7615dfa0f3a12dad9a29ff",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6a47be796453-0001-0000",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I think that's entirely correct, Your Honor. Even in Swain, history was relevant. And to look more broadly, in Arlington Heights, this Court said that history is relevant. So -- and in Miller-El said that history was relevant."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MS. JOHNSON",
      "case_id": "2018-17-9572",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6a47be7964533f8095630376d2ab79acec46a09f6b7615dfa0f3a12dad9a29ff",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6a47be796453-0001-0001",
      "kind": "allegation",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "They said, considering the history, it doesn't alter our opinion, and they pasted in their prior opinion that was history blind."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "JUSTICE GINSBURG",
      "case_id": "2018-17-9572",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6a47be7964533f8095630376d2ab79acec46a09f6b7615dfa0f3a12dad9a29ff",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6a47be796453-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "You say your strongest case is Juror, potential juror, Wright. One of your complaints is that there were many more questions asked of African American potential jurors, but that wasn't so in Wright's case, that she was asked, I think, only three questions. Is that --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MS. JOHNSON",
      "case_id": "2018-17-9572",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6a47be7964533f8095630376d2ab79acec46a09f6b7615dfa0f3a12dad9a29ff",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6a47be796453-0001-0004",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 28,
        "start": 28
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "All of them were African American."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MR. DAVIS",
      "case_id": "2018-17-9572",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6a47be7964533f8095630376d2ab79acec46a09f6b7615dfa0f3a12dad9a29ff",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6a47be796453-0001-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 32,
        "start": 32
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Mississippi Supreme Court's decision in this case was commensurate with Batson and its progeny."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2018-17-9572",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6a47be7964533f8095630376d2ab79acec46a09f6b7615dfa0f3a12dad9a29ff",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6a47be796453-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 47,
        "start": 47
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: But I -- I guess I don't understand how you can say this. In this case, there were three adjudicated Batson violations."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2018-17-9572",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6a47be7964533f8095630376d2ab79acec46a09f6b7615dfa0f3a12dad9a29ff",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6a47be796453-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 49,
        "start": 49
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Did you just say that the same judge who tried the fifth trial also tried the sixth -- the sixth trial?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2018-17-9572",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6a47be7964533f8095630376d2ab79acec46a09f6b7615dfa0f3a12dad9a29ff",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6a47be796453-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 55,
        "start": 55
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: Well, the -- part of Batson was about confidence of the community and the fairness of the criminal justice system, right?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2018-17-9572",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6a47be7964533f8095630376d2ab79acec46a09f6b7615dfa0f3a12dad9a29ff",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6a47be796453-0002-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: You know, I -- one of the first things I did when I found this case was to try to do some research because at least my former state prosecutor's office would have substituted attorneys long before the fifth, sixth trial."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MS. JOHNSON",
      "case_id": "2018-17-9572",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6a47be7964533f8095630376d2ab79acec46a09f6b7615dfa0f3a12dad9a29ff",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6a47be796453-0002-0006",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. JOHNSON: She only exercised peremptories against white jurors."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2018-17-9572",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6a47be7964533f8095630376d2ab79acec46a09f6b7615dfa0f3a12dad9a29ff",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6a47be796453-0002-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 59,
        "start": 59
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: After that, every black juror that was available on the panel was struck --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2018-17-9572",
